### api/health — every request the module serves
#
# Both paths sit outside the /v1 prefix on purpose: an orchestrator's probe
# configuration should not have to change when the API version does.

@baseUrl = {{$dotenv baseUrl}}

###
# @name liveness
# 200 {"status":"ok"}. Answers only "is this process running", so it must stay
# 200 while the database is down -- restarting the api would not help.
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

###
# @name readiness
# 200 {"status":"ok","database":"ok"}, or 503 DATABASE_UNAVAILABLE.
# Answers "can this instance serve traffic", so it fails when the database is
# unreachable and the load balancer should route elsewhere.
#
# To see the failing case:
#   docker compose stop postgres   # readyz -> 503, healthz stays 200
#   docker compose start postgres  # readyz -> 200 again, no api restart
GET {{baseUrl}}/readyz

###
# @name livenessUnderPrefix
# 404. Proof the exclusion is an exclusion and not an addition: the health
# paths must exist at the root and *only* at the root.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/healthz
